# The delivery family's routes are dormant in the shipped cast, which is why
# the book says the supplied record derives floor actualities only through
# confinement. They are not dead: supply a matching receipt and an authorised
# witness who is not the provider, and the floor arrives without a conviction.
#
# This establishes what FOLLOWS from a supplied receipt. It does not establish
# that anybody was fed, housed, treated, materially provided for or visited.
# Material security arrives on its receipt; bodily safety has no receipt route,
# so the same receipt establishes no safety.
:expect-pins 10

? eats(Yenna).
# => TRUE
? dwell(Yenna).
# => TRUE
? healthy(Yenna).
# => TRUE
? suffice(Yenna).
# => TRUE
? secure(Yenna).
# => FALSE
? meets(Yenna).
# => TRUE

# And none of it convicted her, confined her, or touched her word.
? prisoner(Yenna).
# => FALSE
? false(Yenna).
# => FALSE
? lose(Points, Yenna).
# => FALSE
? decide(Yenna, Ballot).
# => TRUE
